nication difficulty but positive crew atmosphere. B has uncooperative and nasty remarks. A has leadership but unorganized.\n\nThus C still seems strongest. Emily can reaffirm C, but incorporate the new info: D's stress resilience is only \"adequate\", not as strong as C's \"keeps calm in a crisis\". Also note that D's moody and loner traits are concerning for crew cooperation. So maintain C.\n\nWe need to give a concise argument, referencing the new info. Also maybe ask about D's reliability? But we can just argue.\n\nThus: \"I continue to support Candidate C as the best overall fit. The new info confirms D only responds adequately to unexpected events, which is less robust than C's proven calmness in crisis. Moreover, D's moody and loner reputation raises crew cooperation concerns, while C creates a positive crew atmosphere despite communication difficulty. Therefore C remains the leading candidate.\"\n\nVote for C.\n\nNow produce final output."}
